# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. Every variable here is OPTIONAL —
# leave one unset and the feature it gates simply ships nothing.
#
# Astro only exposes variables prefixed PUBLIC_ to the built site. That prefix
# means "this value ends up in the HTML" — so only ever put values here that are
# safe to be public. Secrets do NOT belong in this file.

# Cloudflare Web Analytics site token.
# Cloudflare dashboard → Analytics & Logs → Web Analytics → add site → copy the
# token out of the snippet it shows you. It's a public, per-site identifier —
# the beacon is safe to expose, which is exactly why it's PUBLIC_.
# On Cloudflare Pages, set the same variable under Settings → Variables and
# build (add it to BOTH Production and Preview if you want preview traffic too).
PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# Monkeytype ApeKey — OPTIONAL, and a real secret. Note the deliberate lack of a
# PUBLIC_ prefix: PUBLIC_ variables get inlined into the JavaScript sent to
# browsers, which would hand your key to every visitor. This one is read at
# build time only, and nothing but the computed averages ever reaches the HTML.
#
# It is needed ONLY for the average-wpm figures on /type. Everything else in
# that section comes from your public profile and needs no key at all.
# Generate one at Monkeytype → Settings → Ape Keys. On Cloudflare Pages add it
# under Settings → Variables as an ENCRYPTED variable, not a plaintext one.
# Never commit a filled-in value; `.env` is git-ignored, this example file is not.
MONKEYTYPE_APE_KEY=
